  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are two identical sound sources of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>656</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The source&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is located at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> moves anti-clockwise with a uniform speed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;on a circular path around <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. There are three points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> on this path such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> are diametrically opposite while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is equidistant from them. A sound&nbsp;detector is placed at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. The source <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> can move along direction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math>.</p>\n\n<p>[Given: The speed of sound in air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>324</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/2ccb586b-f0a0-4329-b62a-091f10e6cc9f.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 226px;\" /></p>\n<br>When only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is emitting sound and it is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, the frequency of sound measured by the detector in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hz</mi></math> is _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "648",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/5cb2cf53-3ac7-42a1-8ec0-b30bbe403f1e.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 213px;\" /></p><p>Given: Source frequency,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>656</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>.</p><p>Velocity of sound</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>324</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Velocity component of the source moving away from detector along like&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>45</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>Therefore, apparent frequency,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>324</mn><mrow><mn>324</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>656</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>648</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
